If $$f(x)$$ and $$g(x)$$ are two probability density functions, 
$$$f\left( x \right) = \left\{ {\matrix{
   {{x \over a} + 1} &amp; : &amp; { - a \le x &lt; 0}  \cr 
   { - {x \over a} + 1} &amp; : &amp; {0 \le x \le a}  \cr 
   0 &amp; : &amp; {otherwise}  \cr 

 } } \right.$$$
$$$g\left( x \right) = \left\{ {\matrix{
   { - {x \over a}} &amp; : &amp; { - a \le x &lt; 0}  \cr 
   {{x \over a}} &amp; : &amp; {0 \le x \le a}  \cr 
   0 &amp; : &amp; {otherwise}  \cr 

 } } \right.$$$
<p>Which of the following statements is true? </p>
